# C0 vs Render — Worker Memory (CPD-1021 / CPD-1025)

Read the **Worker Memory** block at the top of `STATUS.md` before any git merge or gate/publish work.

**Confluence HOW:** [Server Split — C0/C1+ Boundary](https://aurafluxco.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CP/pages/6881341)

## Three worlds (do not conflate)

| World | Folder | Branch | Deploys to |
|-------|--------|--------|------------|
| **C0 localhost** | `~/cwn-c0` | `c0/main` | pm2 @ localhost:3000 · GitHub **auraflux-c0** |
| **Render production** | `~/cwn-production` | `main` | Render `auraflux-api` + app · GitHub **auraflux-api** |
| **Jira ticket IDs** | — | — | Git commit tags may be wrong (e.g. `cpd-1017` in commits ≠ Jira CPD-1017) |

## Feature graduation — C0 is the proving ground

**New/untested features live on C0 only until Rob declares them customer-ready.** Render prod
(`cwn-production` / `main`) receives features only after they are validated on C0 with real jobs.
Do not port, cherry-pick, or scaffold an unvalidated feature into prod "to get ahead" — the port
happens via an explicit CPD port ticket after Rob approves graduation. (Example: the CPD-1190
Intelligence Engine is C0-only until validated.)

## Never

- Port an untested/unvalidated feature from C0 to prod — graduation requires Rob's approval + a port ticket
- Merge `origin/main` into the C0 branch to "sync" — cherry-pick portable `lib/` fixes only (CPD ticket each)
- Merge C0 branch → `main` without explicit port ticket (PR #637 class mistake)
- Replace C0 `lib/gates/gate5.js` with a production `portal5.js` shim — C0 uses full gate5 + `/uploadposts/status`
- Delete `lib/gates/gate{1,2,3b}.js` without shims — `assembly.js` still `require('./gates/…')`
- `pm2 restart broadcast-sidecar` during a live RTMP-bypass stream (ends YouTube listing)
- Raw `pm2 restart auraflux` during grid — use `bash scripts/safe_restart.sh`

## Reviews

- C0: `bash scripts/aider_session_review_local.sh`
- Render: `bash scripts/aider_session_review.sh`

